- Observable result: the Boolean returned in `<k>`.
- Observable state: all target configuration cells are fixed on both sides;
  the function has no intended external mutation.
- Intended result: true iff some ordered pair of distinct indices satisfies
  `floatLt(absF(subF(x, y)), threshold)`. Ordered-pair existence is equivalent
  to ordinary pair existence here.

